@startuml
title 5G: Control Plane vs User Plane (N2 vs N3)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam participantPadding 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor UE
participant "gNB\n(5G Base Station)" as gNB
participant "AMF\n(Control Plane)" as AMF
participant "SMF\n(Session Control)" as SMF
participant "UPF\n(User Plane)" as UPF
participant "DN\n(Internet)" as DN

== CONTROL PLANE (Signaling) ==
note over UE,SMF
Control Plane = setup + management
- Registration
- 5G-AKA
- Security Mode
- PDU Session Establishment
end note

UE -> gNB: NAS: Registration / Session signaling
gNB -> AMF: N2: Forwards NAS signaling

AMF -> SMF: SBA: Create Session Context\n(Nsmf_PDUSession...)
SMF -> UPF: N4: Install forwarding rules\n(PDR/FAR/QER)

SMF --> AMF: Session Accepted\n(N2 SM info)
AMF -> gNB: N2: Resource Setup Request
gNB --> AMF: Resource Setup Response

AMF -> gNB: NAS: PDU Session Establishment Accept
gNB -> UE: NAS: PDU Session Establishment Accept

== USER PLANE (Actual Data) ==
note over UE,DN
User Plane = real packets
YouTube / WhatsApp / RTP / HTTP etc.
end note

UE <-> gNB: User Data (Radio)
gNB <-> UPF: N3: GTP-U Tunnel\n(User plane packets)
UPF <-> DN: N6: IP traffic to Internet

note bottom
N2 = gNB <-> AMF (Control Plane)
N3 = gNB <-> UPF (User Plane)
N4 = SMF <-> UPF (Rule installation)
N6 = UPF <-> Internet (Data Network)
end note
@enduml
